\section*{3. What the Template is doing}

The LaTeX commands you see in this PDF live here in the Template. The text supplied by Sections and Functions stays content. This keeps formatting separate from reusable or generated content and lets JAW safely escape inserted values.

The readable names in source, such as \texttt{welcome}, \texttt{concepts}, and \texttt{target\_summary}, are symbols. JAW creates and tracks the underlying resource and reference JIDs internally; portable template packages do not contain those JIDs.

